{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "1d5ffcf1-1f34-87a5-8b9d-b273ebcb67c3",
  "created_at": "2026-02-04T13:24:42-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Public Works",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Rachel Rahman",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Kevin Sousa",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T13:21:13-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Public Works, this is Kevin."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T13:21:16-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hi Kevin, my name is Rachel Rahman. I'm calling about a recycling bin that got left with a tag on it saying it was rejected."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T13:21:27-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, a rejected tag on the recycling. Sure. Where's the pickup, what's the address?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T13:21:33-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It's 73 Ayrault Street, up on the Hill. I manage the building, so I'm not there all the time, I just went by this morning and saw it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T13:21:45-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Got it, seventy-three Ayrault. And you said the bin's still sitting at the curb with the tag on it?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T13:21:53-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, still at the curb. The tag has a checked box, something about contamination, but I can't tell what was wrong. Es que, the, um, sorry. I mean the writing is small and it's kind of faded."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T13:22:08-05:00",
      "duration": 18,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No worries at all. Usually that tag means something in the bin wasn't accepted, like plastic bags or food containers that weren't rinsed, or things that don't go in recycling at all. Is there a box checked, or a note handwritten on it?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T13:22:26-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "One box is checked, I think it says bags. Plastic bags. So probably somebody bagged the bottles and cans, the tenants do that sometimes."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T13:22:36-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, that's the most common one. Loose items only, no bagging. So I'll write that down, bagged recyclables, rejected tag, seventy-three Ayrault."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T13:22:46-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. And can you tell me when the next pickup is for that address? I want to fix it before then."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T13:22:55-05:00",
      "duration": 22,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Let me pull up the schedule. Hang on one second. [pause] Okay, Historic Hill, recycling goes out every other week. Your last one was this week, so the next one should be a week from tomorrow, two Thursdays from the, hold on, I'll say it plain: Thursday the nineteenth is what I'm seeing."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T13:23:17-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thursday the nineteenth. Good. So I have time to empty the bags out and put everything loose in the bin."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T13:23:26-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Exactly. Take the tag off, pull everything out of the bags, put it back loose, and set it out that morning or the night before. Bags can go in with regular trash."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T13:23:39-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Sorry, my connection is bad, I'm on a hotspot. My neighbor lent me hers for the day because my internet at the office is down. Si se corta, I mean, if it cuts out, I'm sorry."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T13:23:54-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You're coming through fine. Do you want a callback number on this in case something changes with the schedule?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T13:24:02-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sure. It's 401-555-0194."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T13:24:04-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Four-oh-one, five-five-five, oh-one-nine-four. Got it. Rachel Rahman, seventy-three Ayrault, rejected recycling tag, bagged items, next pickup the nineteenth. Anything else on that?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T13:24:14-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No, that's all. Just one more thing, will the bin get picked up if I leave it as it is now?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T13:24:23-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No, it'll get skipped again until it's been fixed. So take care of it before the nineteenth and you'll be fine."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T13:24:32-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, thank you, Kevin. That's what I needed."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T13:24:36-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You got it. Have a good afternoon."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T13:24:40-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You too. Bye."
    }
  ],
